# Line endings.
#
# core.autocrlf=true on this machine, and with no .gitattributes git was
# converting on every read: `git diff` and `git status` both round-tripped
# CRLF<->LF and printed a warning per file for all 350 baseline fixtures.
#
# It happened to be correct, but "correct because two conversions cancel out"
# is not a property to rest a byte-comparison gate on. The CMS exporter will
# write content/ with \n and the migration is verified by asserting `git diff
# content/` is empty — that check has to compare content, not line endings.
#
# So: normalize to LF in the repository, and check out LF for the trees whose
# bytes are compared or which are written by scripts.
* text=auto eol=lf

# Generated by scripts/ingest-3lines.mjs (soon: the CMS exporter) and by
# scripts/visual-baseline.mjs. Both write \n. Pinning eol=lf means the working
# tree matches what those scripts emit, so a diff is a real difference.
content/**      text eol=lf
baseline/**     text eol=lf
source-content/** text eol=lf

# Hand-authored and served verbatim out of public/ — lib/assets.ts hashes these
# bytes for cache-busting, so a line-ending rewrite would change every URL.
public/assets/**/*.css text eol=lf
public/assets/**/*.js  text eol=lf

*.mjs  text eol=lf
*.ts   text eol=lf
*.tsx  text eol=lf
*.json text eol=lf
*.md   text eol=lf

# Never touch these.
*.png   binary
*.jpg   binary
*.jpeg  binary
*.svg   text eol=lf
*.woff2 binary
*.pdf   binary
*.ico   binary
